<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="097" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Corrected invoice: the old invoice closes Superseded in step 4 (guarded) and its open Signals close Superseded</title>
    <phase>3 Procedures and files (WP3, EB-D-148) — wave W3-F</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 094, 104 and 088 are done</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes the invoice write path and lifecycle (a new close inside the commit transaction), an authorization guard across firms, and append-only Signal history (tags bff-api, auth).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-firm authorization guard, an If-Match re-check inside the transaction, undo that reopens, and a durable idempotent after-step over ontology-owned Signals.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3-F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shares InvoiceSubmissionContracts.cs and InvoiceSubmissionService.cs with 095; run 095 and 097 one after the other.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>094, 104, 088</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, auth, finance, write-path, signals</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement model section 9.1 "Existing invoice" for a corrected invoice: a Submit Invoice request in mode Correction names the old invoice; the new invoice links to it through 104's sprk_supersedesinvoice; the old invoice closes with status reason Superseded (088) inside step 4's transaction; the refusal for Approved, Sent to AP or Paid is checked at intake and re-checked inside step 4 with IfRowVersionMatches; step 5's undo reopens the old invoice; after step 5 passes, every open billing Signal on the old invoice is closed Superseded through SignalWriter.CloseAsync as a durable, resumable, idempotent after-step.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Dataverse write path (ADR-002), ExecuteTransaction with optimistic concurrency, the Finance lifecycle service and the ontology Signal writer. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>A correction produces a new invoice linked to the old one, the old one Superseded in the same transaction, its open Signals closed Superseded after step 5, and every guard and failure path behaving as below; a failed correction leaves the old invoice exactly as it was.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Read projects/ebilling-r1/notes/procedure-and-file-model.md section 9.1 bullet "Existing invoice" and "All or nothing" steps 4-6; notes/procedure-model-reviews.md section 14 (F1-d). Code facts (verified 2026-10-21): SignalWriter.ResolutionSuperseded = 100000003 (Services/Signals/SignalWriter.cs:411); the system close SignalWriter.CloseAsync(signalId, rowVersion, resolutionType, policyCode) (:943), conditional on the Signal's row version, returning SignalCloseOutcome.ChangedSinceRead when a person resolved it since the read; not CloseActedByDecisionAsync (:1020). The after-steps already hold a Superseded close delegate (InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps.cs:134, used at :1159) and read an invoice's open Signals (ReadOpenSignalsAsync, :765). Resume re-runs idempotent after-steps until the terminal status (ResumeAsync :233-269); the totals Retry is the model for a durable step (:226, :266, :484). Transitions belong to InvoiceLifecycleService.TransitionAsync (Services/Finance/InvoiceLifecycleService.cs:306). sprk_supersedesinvoice is read today only by SecureChildLineage and InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuard; 104 writes it for a Returned to Firm predecessor. 088 adds status reason Superseded on sprk_invoice. 094 provides steps 1-6 and the undo.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionContracts.cs (mode Correction, old invoice id)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionService.cs (intake guards)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionPersister.cs (supersedes link, old-invoice close and If-Match guard in the transaction)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/SubmitInvoiceIsolationRerun.cs or its 094 equivalent (undo reopens the old invoice)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps.cs (superseded-Signal close after-step)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/InvoiceLifecycleService.cs (In Review → Superseded in the matrix; a request builder usable inside the transaction)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/Submission/ (InvoiceSubmissionServiceTests, InvoiceSubmissionPersisterTests, InvoiceSubmissionAfterStepsTests) and the lifecycle tests</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/InvoiceSubmissionEndpointsContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 Existing invoice (uac-r2 F1-d)">Every Correction request, before any write: the caller's own Write on the old invoice (gate variant); the old and the new invoice have the same sprk_vendororg and the same core record; the old invoice is not Approved, Sent to AP or Paid (409). A caller without Write gets the uniform Finance answer for an invisible record (no existence leak).</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 step 4">Inside the one transaction: the new invoice's sprk_supersedesinvoice = the old invoice, and the old invoice's close to status reason Superseded carried with IfRowVersionMatches at the version read at the pre-transaction check. A guard fault rolls the whole commit back; the job re-reads the old invoice: now Approved, Sent to AP or Paid → the submission ends Failed with the 409 reason; otherwise the transaction's ordinary Retry.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-06, ADR-002">The Superseded transition is defined only in InvoiceLifecycleService (In Review → Superseded, and Superseded → In Review for the undo only); the persister takes its request from there and writes no status columns of its own.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 step 5 (uac-r2 F1-d)">Step 5's undo list reopens the old invoice to the status it had, with an If-Match write, after the new invoice's rows are deleted; a reopen fault keeps the submission Failed and held until compensation finishes, as 094's undo.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 (ontology-r1 v5.8)">After step 5 passes, every open billing Signal on the old invoice and its lines is closed with SignalWriter.CloseAsync and resolution Superseded (no person recorded); never Dismissed and never CloseActedByDecisionAsync. The step re-reads each Signal; an already-closed Signal counts as success; ChangedSinceRead writes nothing and returns Retry; the next run re-reads (amended 2026-10-30, ontology-r1 OK).</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1 (ontology-r1, durable)">The close is an after-step that runs before the terminal status and returns Retry on any failure, so the existing resume and Retry re-run it after a process death or a failed close. No new writer entry point on SignalWriter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 9.1, (a′)">(a′) does not follow sprk_supersedesinvoice: each invoice is judged by its own source. The new invoice's evaluation raises its own Signals from its snapshot.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md: publish-size delta against a fresh master build; no new package; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="live data">No live Dataverse writes and no deploys.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/procedure-and-file-model.md (section 9.1)</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/procedure-model-reviews.md (section 14)</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/094-submit-invoice.md (written by 094)</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/decisions-log.md (D-34, D-37, D-43)</file>
