      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Superseded Signal close in the after-steps" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps.cs:134, :1159">Reuse the existing delegate; do not add a second binding of CloseAsync.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Durable after-step via Retry" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps.cs:233-269, :484">The totals Retry: a step that fails returns Retry before the terminal status, and resume re-runs it.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare FULL. Read 094's and 104's notes and code (where the transaction is built, how 104 sets sprk_supersedesinvoice) and 088's Superseded status reason value.</step>
    <step order="1">Contracts and intake guards (Write, same firm, same core record, status 409) on both Submit Invoice entries (094's route; 095's from-email if merged).</step>
    <step order="2">Lifecycle: In Review → Superseded and the undo's reopen; a transaction-ready request.</step>
    <step order="3">Persister: link + If-Match close in the transaction; the guard-fault re-read.</step>
    <step order="4">Undo: reopen the old invoice.</step>
    <step order="5">After-step: close the old invoice's open Signals Superseded, idempotent, Retry on failure.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests per the acceptance criteria; seeding proof; build; Finance, Submission and Signals unit tests; full ArchTests; publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="7">Notes in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/097-corrected-invoice.md; update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` after the adversarial review.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a helper that closes one invoice's set of Signals is needed beyond calling the existing CloseAsync delegate per Signal, STOP: it goes through ontology-r1's owner review first (model 9.1).</trigger>
    <trigger>The model defines refusals only for Approved, Sent to AP and Paid. Before coding, ask the owner how a correction of an Inactive invoice (Rejected, Returned to Firm, Cancelled, Superseded) is answered; proposal: 409 invoice_not_correctable, with Returned to Firm resubmissions left to 104's automatic link.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the lifecycle transition cannot be expressed as a request inside the persister's ExecuteTransaction without a second status writer, STOP and report (FR-06 single owner).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>104 links a Returned to Firm predecessor through sprk_supersedesinvoice; InvoiceLifecycleService owns transitions; InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps already binds a Superseded CloseAsync (:134).</existing>
    <extension>Yes: extends 094's operation with a Correction mode, the lifecycle matrix with one transition, the persister's transaction with one guarded update and the after-steps with one step; no new service, route or Signal writer entry point.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A firm's corrected invoice would sit beside the wrong one: both In Review, both counted toward spend, the old one's findings still open and decidable (owner I, 4.x item 2).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">InvoiceSubmissionContracts, InvoiceSubmissionService, InvoiceSubmissionPersister, 094's undo class, InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps, InvoiceLifecycleService</output>
    <output type="test">Updated Submission, lifecycle and Finance contract tests</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/097-corrected-invoice.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Happy path: a Correction of an In Review invoice commits the new invoice with sprk_supersedesinvoice = the old one and the old invoice Superseded in the same transaction; after step 5 passes the old invoice and its lines have no open Signal, each closed with resolution Superseded and no person (test: "a superseded invoice is left with no open Signal").</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Guards before any write: no Write on the old invoice → the uniform not-found answer; a different sprk_vendororg → refused; a different core record → refused; old invoice Approved, Sent to AP or Paid → 409 (one test each).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Race: the old invoice approved between intake and commit → the If-Match guard faults, nothing is committed, the submission ends Failed with the 409 reason, the old invoice stays Approved (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Undo: a step-5 failure deletes the new invoice's rows and reopens the old invoice to In Review; no Signal on the old invoice is closed (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Durable close: the close fails once and the resume completes it; the submission reaches its terminal status only after every open Signal is closed (test: "the close fails once and the resume completes it").</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotent close: an already-closed Signal counts as success; a Signal changed since the read (ChangedSinceRead) writes nothing and returns Retry; the next run re-reads (amended 2026-10-30, ontology-r1 OK) (tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No Signal is closed with resolution Dismissed or through CloseActedByDecisionAsync by this path (test asserts the resolution and the call).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(a′): hiding the old invoice's source does not hide the new invoice, and the reverse (test against 098's predicate).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding proof, recorded in notes: remove the same-sprk_vendororg check → the different-firm test fails; restored.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; Finance, Submission and Signals unit tests and the full ArchTests pass (known pre-existing failures listed by name); publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reviews: adversarial-reviewer twice (auth: cross-firm guard), ontology-r1 for the Signal close, uac-r2 for F1-d. Tracking numbers follow D-37 (firm invoice number kept, new .n via 045). Adding supporting files to an existing invoice is 090's internal upload route, not this task. OWNER 2026-10-21 (re-plan Q2): an Inactive invoice (Rejected, Returned to Firm, Cancelled, Superseded) cannot be changed; a correction against it is refused with 409 before any write. It becomes changeable only if reactivated, and only an admin may reactivate (reactivation itself is out of this task's scope). This answers the escalation trigger on Inactive invoices. ontology-r1 088 gate 2026-10-22, F1 for this task: the Duplicate rule treats a Superseded invoice as live. BillingFactLoader.cs:578-583 maps any status it doesn't list to BillingPriorStatus.Active, and DuplicateHandler.cs:63 compares against Active priors. A corrected invoice keeps the firm's invoice number (D-37) and supersedes the old one, so it raises a Duplicate against the invoice it replaced. Fix: map Superseded (659490005) to null, as Cancelled is. Must-fire test: a corrected invoice whose predecessor is Superseded raises no Duplicate. Must-not-fire: an Active prior with the same number still raises one. BillingFactLoader is under ontology's Services/Signals/Billing path, so ontology-r1 reviews that change.2026-10-22 (088 on dev): sprk_storedfile.sprk_sourcedocument and sprk_sourcecommunication are Restrict, so deleting a Document or Communication that a Stored File points at is refused. Any delete or cleanup path this task adds must expect and handle that refusal (uac-r2 delete design section 15 covers core-record deletes).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load every file in knowledge/files before Step 1. Follow task-execute for rigor, checkpoints and quality gates.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
